@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.11.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.11.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.11.0 (2026-11-24): The Owner asked at 08:02 Istanbul for chapter 11 urgently, so chapter 11 comes before chapter 10. State re-verified after the pause (repository clean, discipline files unchanged at OE 2.41.0 and Lineage 163.0.7, register check passes). The backlog has no way to remove a dependency edge, so the order change is recorded here: the edges TK11_Code_11_Build -> TK11_Release_10_Verify and TK11_Code_10_Build -> TK11_Check_Verify stay in the register as the first plan, and by this change request chapter 11 runs first and chapter 10 after chapter 11's release task. Before the chapter 11 work reaches Done, chapter 10's code story stays Ready, not started."""@en .

ex:CR11_Chapter11First a backlog:ChangeRequest ;
    rdfs:label "Do chapter 11 before chapter 10"@en ;
    backlog:requestsChangeTo ex:Backlog11 ; ;
    backlog:hasChangeRequestRationale "Owner's instruction of 2026-11-24 08:02 Istanbul (content, not a verbatim quotation): he wants chapter 11 urgently." ;
    backlog:hasDisposition backlog:Disp_Accepted .

ex:ST11_Code_11 backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress .
ex:TK11_Code_11_Build backlog:hasState backlog:InProgress ;
    backlog:hasTransitionNote "Starts 2026-11-24 by CR11_Chapter11First, ahead of its recorded dependency on the chapter 10 release task." .
